{"name":"Lumberjack","hex":"#9d4542","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lumberjack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person whose work is to fell trees.","A lumberjacket."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To work as a lumberjack, cutting down trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lumberjack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lumberjack","blocks":[{"text":"Lumberjack is a mostly North American term for workers in the logging industry who perform the initial harvesting and transport of trees. The term usually refers to loggers in the era before 1945 in the United States, when trees were felled using hand tools and dragged by oxen to rivers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/A_lumberjack_standing_at_the_base_of_a_huge_tree_showing_a_cut_in_the_tree%2C_ca.1900_%28CHS-3368%29.jpg/330px-A_lumberjack_standing_at_the_base_of_a_huge_tree_showing_a_cut_in_the_tree%2C_ca.1900_%28CHS-3368%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberjack","wikidata":"Q1124183"},{"title":"Lumberjack (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lumberjack\" is a song by American rapper and producer Tyler, the Creator, released on June 16, 2021, as the lead single from his seventh studio album, Call Me If You Get Lost. The song samples the Gravediggaz track \"2 Cups of Blood\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Lumberjack_by_Tyler%2C_the_Creator_cover_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberjack_(song)","wikidata":"Q107289375"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Jigger_Johnson.jpg/500px-Jigger_Johnson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Jigger_Johnson.jpg/500px-Jigger_Johnson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia